sequenceDiagram
  actor M as MERCHANDISER
  actor A as STORE_ADMIN
  participant API as LayoutCampaignController
  participant S as LayoutCampaignService
  participant F06 as RecommendationService
  participant DB as Store-scoped database
  participant F09 as Active-layout reader

  M->>API: POST /api/campaigns(snapshotId, recommendationIds)
  API->>S: createCampaign
  S->>DB: validate Store snapshot and rank A by distinct transaction frequency
  loop each requested recommendation
    S->>F06: read current recommendation
    F06-->>S: snapshot, APPROVED, readyForConsumption
  end
  S->>DB: insert DRAFT campaign, immutable A, editable B, initial revisions
  DB-->>M: campaign and layout IDs

  M->>API: PUT /api/layouts/{id}/placements(expectedVersion)
  API->>S: save whole recommendation blocks
  S->>F06: recheck current approval and eligibility
  S->>DB: version-check B, save placements/revision, clear decision
  DB-->>M: updated B and version

  opt optional offline simulation while DRAFT
    M->>API: POST /api/campaigns/{id}/simulations(layout versions, date range)
    API->>S: simulate synchronously
    S->>DB: require test start after snapshot end; exclude snapshot training IDs
    S->>DB: persist hash, transaction IDs, assumptions, metrics, exact layout revisions
    DB-->>M: immutable simulated report
  end

  M->>API: record decision then publish
  API->>S: publish(expectedVersion)
  S->>F06: recheck selected layout recommendations
  S->>DB: persist PUBLISHED state and history; storefront unchanged
  DB-->>M: PUBLISHED campaign

  A->>API: POST /api/campaigns/{id}/activate
  API->>S: activate(expectedVersion)
  S->>DB: lock Store row; recheck selected layout; end prior active; activate campaign
  DB-->>A: ACTIVE campaign
  F09->>API: GET /api/storefront/active-layout
  API->>DB: read current ACTIVE campaign and selected layout
  DB-->>F09: selected layout, or default when none is ACTIVE
